    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In contemporary London, social workers Amy and Rosie navigate the stressors and joys of life together, be that work, family or messy dating lives. Leigh and his tight ensemble – Marion Bailey, Paul Jesson, Kate O’Flynn, Alice Bailey Johnson – breathe life into these characters with a deep naturalism that illuminates life’s complexities with warmth, humour and much-needed kindness."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Kristy Matheson"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to book"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tickets start from £10 for all screenings and events in London, with concessions available for many screenings. Booking information and ticket prices .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Booking information and ticket prices",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For non-Members we charge £1 per ticket for online and phone bookings, up to £3 per transaction. There’s no booking fee if you buy tickets at the box office."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you’re aged 16 to 25, sign up for free to BFI 25 and Under for a chance to get £6 tickets (without booking fees) to all screenings and events, subject to availability.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "BFI 25 and Under",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=25-and-under-lff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Missed out?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "More tickets may become available for these screenings before and during the festival. Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues .",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Find out about extra ticket releases and standby queues",
          "url": "https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=tickets-booking-information#extra-ticket-releases"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Our programmers recommend..."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/ink-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Ink"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Danny Boyle brings a seismic moment in Rupert Murdoch’s Fleet Street career blazingly to life, employing the breathtaking style of a story torn from the headlines."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/i-see-buildings-fall-like-lightning-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "I See Buildings Fall Like Lightning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In Clio Barnard’s poignant drama, five childhood friends from Birmingham find their lifelong bonds tested as adulthood brings fractured relationships, unfulfilled dreams and long-buried secrets to light."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/in-the-shadows-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "In the Shadows"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Jasmine Jobson leads a brilliant ensemble in bringing the inspirational story of champion East End boxer Ramla Ali to the screen."
    }
  ]
